### Legislated Tax Code — layout (plan Task 7). The one place that sets the
### order of the tax code's sections, for both hosts: je_tax_code attaches the
### named roots at the foot of this file, and the Tax Code tab, in the Budget
### panel (tab te_tax_code) and the Timeline Extended window, mounts
### te_tax_tab_body, which instances the overview and the two composers. The sections are types in te_tax_overview_widget.gui (the
### overview, the enacted code, the history), te_tax_workbench_widget.gui
### (the workbench and the draft summary), te_tax_review_widget.gui (the
### review), te_tax_politics_widget.gui (passage and passed bills) and here
### (How Tax Legislation Works, and the Help page both codes' links open), in
### the shape of banking_layout_widget.gui.
###
### The journal entry, top to bottom (gui/journal_entry.gui draws container_1,
### the status desc, container_2, the button grid, container_3):
###   container_1  widget_je_tax_code_overview   the overview, always shown,
###                and Open Budget, which opens the tab on these panels
###   status desc  empty while the entry runs (the overview says it all); one
###                line for the inactive entry, which draws nothing else
###   container_2  widget_je_tax_code_status     the live sections, open
###   container_3  widget_je_tax_code_reference  the history and How Tax
###                Legislation Works, a link to the Help page
###                (te_tax_code_help_popup, in gui/te_popups.gui)
###
### Collapse flags say their default: *_closed sections are open until closed,
### *_open ones collapsed until opened (test_tax_code_layout.py).

types te_tax_layout_widget_types
{
	### The live sections, open by default, the ones to watch first and the
	### editor last (GUI audit TAX-14; the owner, 2026-10-27): the bill under
	### debate; the passed bills waiting to take effect; the promises made to
	### pass them (plan Task 12); the code in force; the draft (or Draft a
	### Reform) and its summary; the review of the draft (collapsed until
	### opened). Each monitoring section hides itself when its record is
	### closed, so a quiet code still opens on the Enacted Code. The summary
	### sits in the "draft_summary" block so the Budget tab, which draws it in
	### its fixed_bottom, can leave this copy out. The light code's section
	### comes first: it and the legislated code's never draw together, and
	### placed first it shares the wide layout's first column with the
	### overview (te_tax_wide_sections).
	type te_tax_status_sections = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4
		visible = "[JournalEntry.IsActive]"

		# The light code's rates (te_tax_light_widget.gui; it gates itself).
		te_tax_light_section = {}
		# The legislated code's sections, hidden under the light setting.
		flowcontainer = {
			visible = "[Not( GetScriptedGui('te_tax_show_light_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End ) )]"
			direction = vertical
			parentanchor = hcenter
			ignoreinvisible = yes
			spacing = 4

			te_tax_politics_section = {}
			te_tax_pending_section = {}
			te_tax_obligations_section = {}
			te_tax_enacted_table = {}
			te_tax_workbench_section = {}
			block "draft_summary" {
				te_tax_draft_summary = {}
			}
			te_tax_review_section = {}
		}
	}

	### "How Tax Legislation Works": a link at the foot of the panel to the Help
	### page (style guide rule 1; spec 2026-11-02-charts-help-national-info
	### § 5.2). Its header alone, which opens te_tax_code_help_popup (te_popup =
	### help_tax_code) instead of expanding; it keeps its name and its place in
	### the composers, under their Not(light) wrappers. The Light code's own
	### link, te_tax_light_how_section, opens the same page, and so does the
	### "?" in the tab's header.
	type te_tax_how_section = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 2

		te_tax_section_header = {
			tooltip = "te_help_link_tt"
			blockoverride "left_text" {
				text = "te_tax_how_header"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick" {
				onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Set('te_popup', 'help_tax_code')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showmore" {
				visible = no
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showless" {
				visible = no
			}
		}
	}

	### The Help page, one for both codes: How the Light Tax Code Works while the
	### Light code is in force (te_tax_show_light_sgui), How Tax Legislation Works
	### otherwise, each one heading per topic; the popup's title follows the same
	### gate. The live sections say what is in force; this says how it got there
	### and how it changes. The passage rule's numbers (share, legitimacy, debate
	### days, thresholds, due-month range, reschedule delay) are read from its own
	### script values (te_tax_support_values.txt), so those follow the rule. The
	### Customs topic and the customs half of the monthly line show only under the
	### customs option (te_tax_show_customs_option_sgui). Three facts are written
	### out in both the loc and the script and CAN drift: the sunset offsets
	### 6/12/24/36/60 (te_tax_dr_sunset_*), a minor bill's "two taxes, two steps"
	### (te_tax_bill_set_minor, te_tax_gen_bill_small_steps) and regional relief's
	### "at most three" states (the schema's cap, which Task 11's state selection
	### enforces; the Enacted Code's relief hover says it too). Change the loc
	### with them.
	### It reads GetPlayer only, as the section did, so it opens from any host
	### (test_te_help_pages.py). Instanced only by te_tax_code_help_popup.
	type te_tax_code_help_body = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4

		### Under the Light code: How the Light Tax Code Works.
		flowcontainer = {
			visible = "[GetScriptedGui('te_tax_show_light_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End )]"
			direction = vertical
			ignoreinvisible = yes
			spacing = 4

			te_tax_subheader = {
				blockoverride "subheader_margin" {}
				blockoverride "subheader_text" {
					text = "te_tax_lt_how_sub_rates"
				}
			}
			te_tax_note = {
				text = "te_tax_lt_how_rates"
			}
			te_tax_note = {
				text = "te_tax_lt_how_law"
			}

			te_tax_subheader = {
				blockoverride "subheader_text" {
					text = "te_tax_lt_how_sub_level"
				}
			}
			te_tax_note = {
				text = "te_tax_lt_how_level"
			}

			te_tax_subheader = {
				blockoverride "subheader_text" {
					text = "te_tax_lt_how_sub_groups"
				}
			}
			te_tax_note = {
				text = "te_tax_lt_how_groups"
			}
			te_tax_note = {
				text = "te_tax_lt_how_relief"
			}

			te_tax_subheader = {
				blockoverride "subheader_text" {
					text = "te_tax_lt_how_sub_native"
				}
			}
			te_tax_note = {
				text = "te_tax_lt_how_native"
			}
			te_tax_note = {
				text = "te_tax_lt_how_ai"
			}
		}

		### Otherwise: How Tax Legislation Works.
		flowcontainer = {
			visible = "[Not( GetScriptedGui('te_tax_show_light_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End ) )]"
			direction = vertical
			ignoreinvisible = yes
			spacing = 4

			te_tax_subheader = {
				blockoverride "subheader_margin" {}
				blockoverride "subheader_text" {
					text = "te_tax_how_sub_drafting"
				}
			}
			te_tax_note = {
				text = "te_tax_how_drafting"
			}
			te_tax_note = {
				text = "te_tax_how_drafting_baseline"
			}

			te_tax_subheader = {
				blockoverride "subheader_text" {
					text = "te_tax_how_sub_passage"
				}
			}
			te_tax_note = {
				text = "te_tax_how_passage"
			}
			te_tax_note = {
				text = "te_tax_how_passage_rule"
			}
			te_tax_note = {
				text = "te_tax_how_passage_offers"
			}
			te_tax_note = {
				text = "te_tax_how_passage_force"
			}

			te_tax_subheader = {
				blockoverride "subheader_text" {
					text = "te_tax_how_sub_commencement"
				}
			}
			te_tax_note = {
				text = "te_tax_how_commencement"
			}
			te_tax_note = {
				text = "te_tax_how_commencement_sunset"
			}
			te_tax_note = {
				text = "te_tax_how_commencement_held"
			}

			te_tax_subheader = {
				blockoverride "subheader_text" {
					text = "te_tax_how_sub_promises"
				}
			}
			te_tax_note = {
				text = "te_tax_how_promises"
			}
			te_tax_note = {
				text = "te_tax_how_promises_kinds"
			}
			te_tax_note = {
				text = "te_tax_how_promises_outcomes"
			}

			te_tax_subheader = {
				blockoverride "subheader_text" {
					text = "te_tax_how_sub_replaces"
				}
			}
			te_tax_note = {
				text = "te_tax_how_replaces"
			}
			# Under the customs option the monthly sync sets tariffs too.
			te_tax_note = {
				text = "[SelectLocalization( GetScriptedGui('te_tax_show_customs_option_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End ), 'te_tax_how_replaces_monthly_customs', 'te_tax_how_replaces_monthly' )]"
			}
			te_tax_note = {
				text = "te_tax_how_replaces_views"
			}

			# Customs, under the customs option only (final review B-I1).
			te_tax_subheader = {
				visible = "[GetScriptedGui('te_tax_show_customs_option_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End )]"
				blockoverride "subheader_text" {
					text = "te_tax_how_sub_customs"
				}
			}
			te_tax_note = {
				visible = "[GetScriptedGui('te_tax_show_customs_option_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End )]"
				text = "te_tax_how_customs"
			}
			te_tax_note = {
				visible = "[GetScriptedGui('te_tax_show_customs_option_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End )]"
				text = "te_tax_how_customs_sync"
			}
		}
	}

	### The Help page's popup, in te_popups (gui/te_popups.gui).
	type te_tax_code_help_popup = te_ui_help_popup {
		blockoverride "popup_visible" {
			visible = "[GetVariableSystem.HasValue('te_popup', 'help_tax_code')]"
		}
		blockoverride "popup_title" {
			text = "[SelectLocalization( GetScriptedGui('te_tax_show_light_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End ), 'te_tax_lt_how_header', 'te_tax_how_header' )]"
		}
		blockoverride "popup_list" {
			te_tax_code_help_body = {}
		}
	}

	### The record, then how it all works: the history, collapsed (a list of
	### past items), and How Tax Legislation Works, the link, last. The light
	### code's How comes first, as its section does in te_tax_status_sections,
	### so the wide layout's second column ends on it.
	type te_tax_reference_sections = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4
		visible = "[JournalEntry.IsActive]"

		# How the Light Tax Code Works (te_tax_light_widget.gui; it gates itself).
		te_tax_light_how_section = {}
		# The legislated code's history and explanation, hidden under the light
		# setting, which keeps no history.
		flowcontainer = {
			visible = "[Not( GetScriptedGui('te_tax_show_light_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End ) )]"
			direction = vertical
			parentanchor = hcenter
			ignoreinvisible = yes
			spacing = 4

			te_tax_history_section = {}
			te_tax_how_section = {}
		}
	}

	### The Tax Code tab's body (spec 2026-11-02-te-window-wide-mode § 9.1):
	### te_system_tab_frame with its blocks filled, mounted by the Budget
	### panel's Tax Code tab and the Timeline Extended window's. The overview
	### and the two composers inside te_tax_tab_layout, which a wide mount
	### overrides, then the frame's Open Journal Entry in the tab's row font.
	### The types read the player's country (GetPlayer), so the datacontext
	### serves only the IsActive gates and the link. Each frame draws the
	### draft and bill summaries in its fixed_bottom, so the live sections
	### leave their own copy out ("draft_summary").
	type te_tax_tab_body = te_system_tab_frame {
		blockoverride "tab_header" {
			default_header = {
				using = default_list_position
				blockoverride "text" {
					text = "je_tax_code"
				}
				te_help_button = {
					onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Set('te_popup', 'help_tax_code')]"
				}
			}
		}

		blockoverride "tab_gate" {
			visible = "[GetScriptedGui('te_budget_tax_tab_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End )]"
		}

		blockoverride "tab_entry" {
			datacontext = "[GetPlayerJournalEntry('je_tax_code')]"
		}

		blockoverride "tab_content" {
			block "te_tax_tab_layout" {
				te_tax_overview_panel = {}
				te_tax_status_sections = {
					blockoverride "draft_summary" {}
				}
				te_tax_reference_sections = {}
			}
		}

		blockoverride "tab_open_journal_font" {
			using = te_tax_fontsize_row
		}

		blockoverride "tab_open_journal_tooltip" {
			tooltip = "te_tax_open_journal_tt"
		}
	}

	### The Timeline Extended window's full-screen Tax Code tab (spec
	### 2026-11-02-te-window-wide-mode § 7): the tab's layout read down one
	### row of three columns of 520 (te_ui_columns_three). Under the full
	### code: the overview and the bills and promises to watch, then the code
	### in force, the workbench and the review, then the history and How Tax
	### Legislation Works. Under the light code: the overview and the light
	### section, then the light How, and the third column empty (it keeps its
	### 520). Each section keeps its narrow gates, the wrappers repeating the
	### composers' and the full code's Not( light ), with their spacing; a run
	### of the full code's sections alone takes both in one And, so under the
	### light code its wrapper hides and leaves no gap above the light How. The
	### draft summary is in the window's footer, so it is left out here as the
	### tab body leaves it out. The window's wide mount puts it in
	### te_tax_tab_layout (gen_te_systems_window.py);
	### test_tax_code_layout.WideTest checks it against the narrow layout.
	type te_tax_wide_sections = te_ui_columns_three {
		blockoverride "column_1" {
			te_tax_overview_panel = {}

			flowcontainer = {
				visible = "[JournalEntry.IsActive]"
				direction = vertical
				parentanchor = hcenter
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				spacing = 4

				te_tax_light_section = {}
				flowcontainer = {
					visible = "[Not( GetScriptedGui('te_tax_show_light_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End ) )]"
					direction = vertical
					parentanchor = hcenter
					ignoreinvisible = yes
					spacing = 4

					te_tax_politics_section = {}
					te_tax_pending_section = {}
					te_tax_obligations_section = {}
				}
			}
		}

		blockoverride "column_2" {
			flowcontainer = {
				visible = "[And( JournalEntry.IsActive, Not( GetScriptedGui('te_tax_show_light_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End ) ) )]"
				direction = vertical
				parentanchor = hcenter
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				spacing = 4

				te_tax_enacted_table = {}
				te_tax_workbench_section = {}
				te_tax_review_section = {}
			}

			flowcontainer = {
				visible = "[JournalEntry.IsActive]"
				direction = vertical
				parentanchor = hcenter
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				spacing = 4

				te_tax_light_how_section = {}
			}
		}

		blockoverride "column_3" {
			flowcontainer = {
				visible = "[And( JournalEntry.IsActive, Not( GetScriptedGui('te_tax_show_light_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( GetPlayer.MakeScope ).End ) ) )]"
				direction = vertical
				parentanchor = hcenter
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				spacing = 4

				te_tax_history_section = {}
				te_tax_how_section = {}
			}
		}
	}
}

### ==========================================================================
### JOURNAL ENTRY ROOTS (je_tax_code.txt). Bare wrappers that repeat the
### composers' IsActive gate: je_tax_code has is_shown_when_inactive, so the
### panel can open for a country whose entry has not activated yet and so has
### none of the code's variables, and an inactive entry's containers must
### collapse (gotcha #14). Each root is exactly a section's width (520): a
### wrapper sized by its content is centred at its first width and drifts
### once a hidden row appears (style guide rule 8).
### ==========================================================================
flowcontainer = {
	name = "widget_je_tax_code_overview"
	visible = "[JournalEntry.IsActive]"
	direction = vertical
	parentanchor = hcenter
	ignoreinvisible = yes
	minimumsize = { 520 -1 }
	spacing = 6

	te_tax_overview_panel = {}

	# The tab carries the same panels, and later the workbench, so the entry
	# links to it. OpenPanelTab with a mod tab name is the top bar's Banking
	# phase icon's shape (banking_dashboard_widget.gui, 'te_banking'); if it
	# does not select the tab in game, the fallback is OpenPanel('budget'),
	# which opens Budget and leaves the player to click the tab.
	button = {
		using = default_button
		using = te_tax_fontsize_row
		parentanchor = hcenter
		size = { 480 32 }
		text = "te_tax_open_budget"
		tooltip = "te_tax_open_budget_tt"
		onclick = "[InformationPanelBar.OpenPanelTab('budget', 'te_tax_code')]"
	}
}

flowcontainer = {
	name = "widget_je_tax_code_status"
	visible = "[JournalEntry.IsActive]"
	direction = vertical
	parentanchor = hcenter
	ignoreinvisible = yes
	minimumsize = { 520 -1 }

	te_tax_status_sections = {}
}

flowcontainer = {
	name = "widget_je_tax_code_reference"
	visible = "[JournalEntry.IsActive]"
	direction = vertical
	parentanchor = hcenter
	ignoreinvisible = yes
	minimumsize = { 520 -1 }

	te_tax_reference_sections = {}
}
